For purposes of this License:

**"Software"** means the JObfuscate software, including its source code, compiled binaries, command-line interface (CLI), graphical user interface (GUI), libraries, modules, scripts, configuration files, documentation, and other materials distributed by the Copyright Holder as part of the Software.

**"Source Code"** means the human-readable source code of the Software and any accompanying files reasonably necessary to modify and build the Software.

**"Compiled Version"** means any executable, binary, JAR, native executable, packaged application, installer, or other machine-readable form of the Software produced from the Source Code.

**"Copyright Holder"** means Liam Kubicki and any party subsequently authorized by the Copyright Holder to issue licenses for the Software.

**"Non-Commercial Use"** means use of the Software that is not conducted for a Commercial Purpose.

**"Commercial Purpose"** means a purpose that directly or indirectly:

1. generates revenue, compensation, profit, or other monetary benefit for the user or another party;

2. supports, operates, develops, maintains, or contributes to a business or commercial organization;

3. is performed as part of paid employment, contract work, consulting, freelancing, or other compensated services;

4. is performed for a product, service, application, game, plugin, library, mod, server, website, or other software that is sold, licensed, subscribed to, monetized, or otherwise provided for compensation;

5. provides obfuscation, transformation, packaging, build, protection, or related services to another person or organization for compensation;

6. is performed as part of a commercial software development, build, release, or distribution pipeline; or

7. otherwise provides a material commercial benefit to a business, organization, or revenue-generating project.

**"Commercial User"** means any individual, company, organization, partnership, corporation, or other legal or natural person that uses the Software for a Commercial Purpose.

**"Commercial License"** means a separate license granted by the Copyright Holder permitting Commercial Use of the Software.

**"Authorized User"** means an employee, contractor, agent, or other person authorized by a Commercial License holder to use the Software on that license holder's behalf.

